PURPOSE
H78 showed that cells can discover:
which primitive transformations participate in a useful causal pathway.

H79 asks the next structural question:

CAN A REPEATEDLY USEFUL PRIMITIVE SEQUENCE
BECOME A NEW COMPACT MACRO-OPERATOR?

And:

CAN THAT COMPILED STRUCTURE REMAIN REVERSIBLE
WHEN THE useful pathway changes?

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- invent new primitive semantics;
- freeze a compiler/chunker;
- freeze macro size = 2;
- prove real Yggdrasil should execute fused kernels;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

