MACRO NOMINATION
A contiguous primitive pair may be nominated when:
it repeatedly appears on successful terminal provenance.

Primary threshold:
250 successful ancestry observations.

Nominated phase-1 macro:

M8:
R -> B

representing:

R -> A -> B.

Nominated phase-2 macro:

M9:
R -> C

representing:

R -> A -> C.

Macro execution counts as:
one local transform

instead of:
two.

Macro synthetic action cost:
0.18

vs:
0.15 + 0.15
for the two primitives.

Thus:
compilation has a small efficiency advantage.

