OUTSIDE-STATUS-QUO IMPLICATION
The developmental genome may not need to contain:
every mature computational pathway directly.

It can contain:

primitive transformations
+
rules for causal chunk nomination
+
rules for reversible compilation.

Repeated useful cognition can:
crystallize into faster local structure.

Novel conditions can:
fall back to:
slower generative composition.

This resembles:
developmental compilation

more than:
fixed neural architecture.

DECISION
AR-H79 is POSITIVE WITH A HARD IRREVERSIBLE-COMPILATION FAILURE.

Supported synthetically:

- repeated useful primitive compositions can be compiled into lower-action macro-operators;
- macro execution reduces transformation overhead;
- irreversible compilation destroys future recombinability;
- retaining primitives allows recovery after pathway change;
- stale macros still slow adaptation if execution authority is not separately controlled;
- fast reversible macro trust restores rapid adaptation;
- new macros can develop after the environment changes.

Not demonstrated:

- arbitrary macro length;
- nested macro hierarchy;
- real code-generation speedup;
- memory cost of many macros;
- macro credit under long delayed consequence;
- safe shared macro distribution across cells.

NEXT HIGH-VALUE MOVE
AR-H80 — MACRO ECOLOGY / HIERARCHICAL CHUNK EXPLOSION CONTROL

If every repeated useful sequence can become:
a macro,

the organism may create:
too many compiled fragments.

Question:

How should macro structures compete for:
permanent memory
and
execution authority?

Candidate pressures:

- recurrence frequency;
- functional value;
- action savings;
- context breadth;
- compositional reuse;
- storage cost;
- staleness.

Compare:

A.
compile every successful chunk;

B.
fixed macro-count cap;

C.
value-per-memory macro price;

D.
shared sub-chunk reuse;

E.
nested macro hierarchy;

F.
environment switching among recurring tasks.

Desired:

common reusable sequence
->
retained.

rare task-specific chunk
->
retired or reconstructed.

overlapping macros
->
share substructure rather than:
duplicate permanent state.

This connects:
H79 program compilation

with:
H34-H40 generative retirement
and
H46-H49 memory pricing.

